text.section:
The board shall have the power to:

Establish rules and regulations governing the operation of the jail or jail farm not inconsistent with standards of the State Board of Local and Regional Jails;


Purchase land for the jail or jail farm for joint ownership by the participating political subdivisions with the approval of the local governing bodies;


Provide for all necessary stock, equipment and structures for the jail or jail farm within the budget approved therefor by the participating political subdivisions; and


Appoint a superintendent of such jail or jail farm and necessary jail officers therefor who shall serve at the pleasure of the board.
				The political subdivisions establishing a regional jail or jail farm shall pay their pro rata costs for land, stock, equipment and structures.
